## Why This Is Asked
Tests must cover internationalization, accessibility, and end-to-end flow in a single system. This question probes test design for localization, RTL, and deterministic reproducibility across many locales.

## Key Concepts
- Locale/RTL handling, i18n data, currency/date formatting
- E2E test parametrization, deterministic seeds, mocks
- Accessibility tree verification in dynamic UIs
- Network throttling and flakiness handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright pseudo-test outline for locale switch
test('e2e locale switch', async ({ page, browserRoom }) => {
  const ctx = await browser.newContext({ locale: 'en-US' });
  const p = page;
  await p.goto('/');
  // switch locale mid-session
  await p.click('#locale-switch');
  await p.click('text=العربية');
  // continue flow
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you isolate locale data seeds per locale to avoid cross-test contamination?
- How would you validate that translations load within a 2-second window in a flaky network scenario?

