## Why This Is Asked
Tests data isolation, asynchronous ETL, eventual consistency, and idempotency in a real-world multi-tenant dashboard.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation
- Mocking external data sources
- Idempotent operations
- Eventual consistency and latency
- Regional replication and failover

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright-like sketch
test('dataset ETL end-to-end with tenant isolation', async ({page}) => {
  const tenant = await createTenant();
  const dsId = `ds-${Date.now()}`;
  await loginAsTenantUser(tenant);
  await page.goto('/datasets');
  await page.fill('#name', dsId);
  await page.click('#create');
  // mock external sources and trigger ETL via API
  await mockExternalDataForTenant(tenant, dsId);
  await triggerETL(dsId);
  await waitForDashboardData(tenant, dsId);
  // idempotency check
  await page.click('#create', {force:true});
  await waitForDashboardData(tenant, dsId);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate data correctness if ETL shows partial results due to a region outage?
- What metrics would you collect to monitor test determinism across runs?

## Why This Is Asked
E2E with ML serving is common in production; tests must cover routing, feature delivery, latency, drift, and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Canary vs Shadow routing
- Feature store integration and data drift monitoring
- Multi-region consistency and rollback triggers
- Observability and SLO validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-test harness for ML-serving end-to-end
async function runETest(seed) {
  await seedFeatureStore(seed);
  const a = await requestModel('A', seed);
  const b = await requestModel('B', seed);
  assertClose(a.pred, b.pred, tol=0.01);
  assertLatency(b.latency, 400);
  // simulate drift and verify rollback path
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement drift thresholds and alerting?  
- How would you test rollback under partial failure (region loss)?

